# encoding: utf-8
=begin

  InjuryWatch watches the people in your room and shows who needs healing.

  It is mainly for empaths who want a small triage list while they are helping
  a room. It quietly checks people as they arrive, updates when people leave
  or change, and shows simple labels like OK, Bleeding, Scarred, and Dead.

  Dead people stay at the top and show what still needs healing, such as
  "Dead - Bleeding". Likely empaths are marked with [E] because they can
  usually heal themselves.

  The display can be a StormFront, Wrayth, or Warlock dock window, a GTK popup window, or
  simple story-window text. If the display looks wrong, use text mode.

       author: Mystienne
         game: gs
         tags: heal, empath, triage, injury, window, hud
      version: 0.2.6
     required: Lich >= 5.11.0
        email: Mystienne@mystienne.com
      discord: Mystienne

=end

no_kill_all
no_pause_all
hide_me
silence_me

require 'set'

# Watches the room and keeps the InjuryWatch triage display updated.
#
# Keeps script state, display helpers, command text, and appraise handling out
# of the global namespace.
module InjuryWatch

  VERSION = '0.2.6'

  CHECK_EVERY = 1.0

  HELP_TEXT = <<~HELP
    InjuryWatch #{VERSION}

    Watches the room and shows who needs healing.

    Commands:
      ;injurywatch
          Start watching the room.

      ;injurywatch help
          Show this help.

      ;injurywatch setup
          Open the display setup window.

      ;injurywatch debug
          Start with debug messages turned on.

      ;injurywatch display=dock
          Use the XML dock window (StormFront, Wrayth, or Warlock) for this run.

      ;injurywatch display=popup
          Use the GTK popup window for this run.

      ;injurywatch display=text
          Print triage changes in the story window for this run.

      ;injurywatch version
          Show the script version.

      ;injurywatch changelog
          Show recent changes by day.

      ;send injurywatch refresh
          Re-check injured people.

      ;send injurywatch refresh room
          Re-check everyone in the room.

    Display settings:
      ;vars set injurywatch_display=dock
      ;vars set injurywatch_display=popup
      ;vars set injurywatch_display=text
      ;vars delete injurywatch_display

    Notes:
      Dock mode works in StormFront, Wrayth, and Warlock. Avalon users should
      use popup or text.

      FLAG DIALOGS OFF hides appraise popup windows from silent appraisals.
      FLAG DIALOGS ON turns them back on.
  HELP

